{"n": 896, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "896.webp", "text": "Procedures:\nClean the area to be repaired with a cement remover.\n\nNote:\nLet cleaned surface dry at room temperature about 10 minutes before\napplication of the repair material,\n\nGrind down repalr surface (grain size P 80).\n\nGrind damaged surface In V-shape (grain size P 36).\n\nif damage continues through the plastic, clean the back side of the repair\nsurface with a cement remover and grind (grain size P 36).\n\n3. Remove grinding abrasion.\n\nPaste aluminum adhesive tape above the damaged surtace on the front.\n\n5. Cut glass grid fabric to size for the reapir surface.\n\n. Mix repair material to the Instructions supplied with It.\n\n7. Apply a coat of repair material on the back of the repair surtace. Apply the\nglass grid fabric, cover it with repair material and let It harden at room\n\ntemperature about 20 minutes.\n\n8. Pull off aluminum adhesive tape and, If necessary, grind down and clean the\n\nrepaired surface again.\n\n9. Apply coat of repair material on the front and let It harden.\n\n10. Grind down the repaired surtace (grain size P 80) and smooth with grain\nsize P 180.\n\nimportant!\nIt Is absolutely necessary to use the specified grain size grinding materials\nIn order to guarantee perfect results (thermal development).\n\n51-101\n\nProcedures for Repairing Minor Brulses and Scratches:\n\n1\n\n2.\n\nGrind down damaged zone generously (down Into the subtrate) with dry\nsanding paper (grain size: 400 - 500).\n\nClean ground zone with a plastic cleaner.\n\n3. Apply coat of plastic adhesion solution.\n\nApply several coats of BMW Rapid Filler + 20 % BMW Softtace Additive on\nthe cleaned surface until the shape of the part can be restored after grinding.\n\n. Grind down filled surface with wet sanding paper (grain size: 800 - 1000}.\n\nContinue as described in point 3, if graund through spots or damaged spots\nare still visible.\n\nGrind down entire part It applicable (depending on extent of damage).\n\nApply final coat of paint with two-component BMW acrylic paint + 20 % BMW\nsoitface additive; for double-layer metallic paint finishes 20 % softlace\nadditive is mixed with the BMW acrylic clear lacquer.\n\nRefer to the BMW Paint Spraying Manual for spraying Instructions,\nmaterials and so on.\n\n‘Cauton!\n\nUse mask and make sure of sufficient ventilation.\n\nConform with accident prevention stipulations for working with paints.\nConform with local and national legislation concerning safety at work and\naccident prevention as well as working material ordinances.\n\nRefer to instructions supplied by the manufacturers!", "words": [["Procedures:", 0.0241, 0.0855, 0.0899, 0.0986], ["Clean", 0.0422, 0.1177, 0.0734, 0.1308], ["the", 0.0774, 0.119, 0.093, 0.1295], ["area", 0.097, 0.1203, 0.1191, 0.1295], ["to", 0.1231, 0.119, 0.1332, 0.1308], ["be", 0.1377, 0.119, 0.1497, 0.1295], ["repaired", 0.1538, 0.1177, 0.1985, 0.1321], ["with", 0.2025, 0.1177, 0.2246, 0.1295], ["a", 0.2276, 0.119, 0.2337, 0.1295], ["cement", 0.2377, 0.1177, 0.2774, 0.1282], ["remover.", 0.2814, 0.119, 0.3291, 0.1282], ["Note:", 0.0432, 0.1519, 0.0704, 0.1637], ["Let", 0.0412, 0.1624, 0.0588, 0.1854], ["cleaned", 0.0643, 0.1624, 0.103, 0.1854], ["surface", 0.1085, 0.1624, 0.1467, 0.1854], ["dry", 0.1523, 0.1624, 0.1688, 0.1854], ["at", 0.1729, 0.1624, 0.1849, 0.1854], ["room", 0.1889, 0.1624, 0.2131, 0.1854], ["temperature", 0.2181, 0.1624, 0.2834, 0.1854], ["about", 0.2884, 0.1624, 0.3171, 0.1854], ["10", 0.3231, 0.1663, 0.3342, 0.1775], ["minutes", 0.3397, 0.1624, 0.3799, 0.1854], ["before", 0.3854, 0.1624, 0.4211, 0.1854], ["application", 0.0432, 0.1854, 0.2206, 0.2012], ["of", 0.1055, 0.1828, 0.1151, 0.2038], ["the", 0.1201, 0.1828, 0.1352, 0.2038], ["repair", 0.1402, 0.1828, 0.1714, 0.2038], ["material,", 0.1764, 0.1828, 0.2221, 0.2038], ["Grind", 0.0442, 0.2314, 0.0729, 0.2531], ["down", 0.0794, 0.2314, 0.103, 0.2531], ["repalr", 0.1101, 0.2354, 0.1407, 0.2505], ["surface", 0.